  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n\nThe proposed approach combines binary search with semidefinite relaxation to explore the solution space more thoroughly. By first considering a binary h, we simplify the problem while maintaining key constraints. We then gradually relax towards the full optimization problem, leveraging the structure discovered in the binary phase.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n\nLet h: [0,2] \u2192 {0,1}, with \u222bh = 1. The overlap O_k for shift k is:\n\n$$\nO_k = \\sum_{i=0}^{n-k} h_i (1 - h_{i+k})\n$$\n\nOur goal is to minimize:\n\n$$\nC_5 = \\max_k \\frac{O_k}{n}\n$$\n\nWe formulate the problem as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\min_{\\{h_i\\}, C} & \\quad C \\\\\n\\text{s.t.} & \\quad \\sum_{i=0}^{n-1} h_i = n / 2 \\\\\n& \\quad O_k \\leq C n \\quad \\forall k \\\\\n& \\quad h_i \\in \\{0,1\\}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAfter finding a binary solution, we relax $h_i \\in [0,1]$ and add a penalty term to favor sparse solutions.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n\na. Initialize: Start with a binary h either from initial_h_values, randomly generated, or through alternating blocks.\n\nb. Binary phase:\n   - Formulate and solve the LP with binary h.\n   - Track shifts k with high overlap.\n\nc. Relaxation phase:\n   - Solve a convex problem allowing h \u2208 [0,1], penalizing deviations from the binary solution.\n   - Iteratively tighten constraints for worst shifts.\n\nd. Validation and feasibility checks ensure constraints are satisfied at each step.\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n\n- Initialize with alternating blocks or random binary vectors.\n- Vary the penalty weight for the relaxation phase.\n- Adjust the number of iterations for the tightening loop.\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n\nThe approach is budgeted for 600s with:\n- ~100 iterations of the tightening loop.\n- Each iteration: binary LP (fast) + convex solve (moderate).\n- Early termination if target achieved.\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n\n- Ensure h is feasible: h \u2208 [0,1], sums to n/2.\n- Compute exact C\u2085 using the problem's evaluator.\n- Store the best feasible solution throughout.",
